    "content": "\"CW\" most commonly stands for CBS and Warner Bros., representing the television network created by their partnership in 2006. It is also widely used online to mean Content Warning or Trigger Warning to alert viewers about sensitive content, or in technical contexts for Clockwise or Continuous Wave. Here are the most common meanings: Television Network (The CW): Formed by the merger of UPN and The WB, combining the first letters of its founders, CBS and Warner Bros.. Social Media/Online: Content Warning or Trigger Warning (preface to a post warning of sensitive topics). Technical/Directions: Clockwise (often used with CCW for counterclockwise). Radio/Tech: Continuous Wave (a method of radio transmission). Business/General: Common Wisdom or Chemical Weapon.",
